        "original_id": "8cb831c3-46ce-5e0c-a5ae-70e2a34a7c0c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Teams: 1963 Texas Longhorns football team\n- People: Tommy Nobis, Roger Staubach\n- Organizations: University of Texas at Austin, Atlanta Falcons, National Football League\n- Events: 1963 college football season, 1964 Cotton Bowl Classic, Heisman Trophy\n\nFacts:\n- The 1963 Texas Longhorns football team represented the University of Texas at Austin in the 1963 college football season.\n- Thomas Henry Nobis Jr. was born on September 20, 1943.\n- Tommy Nobis was the only sophomore starter on the 1963 Texas Longhorns football team.\n- The 1963 Texas Longhorns football team defeated #2 Navy 28–6 in the 1964 Cotton Bowl Classic.\n- Roger Staubach led Navy and was a Heisman Trophy winner when Navy lost to the 1963 Texas Longhorns football team in the 1964 Cotton Bowl Classic.\n- Tommy Nobis later played linebacker in the National Football League for eleven seasons with the Atlanta Falcons.",
